# Redeclaration in the same scope rejected

Verifies two `let` declarations of the same name in one lexical scope are
rejected. The second declaration is a redeclaration, not shadowing, because
both bindings belong to the same scope.

>>> source
let x: int = 10
let x: int = 20

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: binding `x` is already declared in this scope at Span { start: 16, end: 31 }

<<< exit
1
